module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.MoreMorphisms.FppfApplication.IntegralExtensionCounterexampleSections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.MoreMorphisms.FppfApplication.IntegralSurjectiveExtension

/-!
# Tag 0CNX is false for a general open subscheme

A surjective integral morphism over a *quasi-compact* open subscheme extends to a surjective
integral morphism over the whole scheme; this is
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_integral_surjective_extension`, the corrected (retrocompact) form of
[Stacks, Tag 0CNX], whose general statement is false. Here we show the restriction is necessary:
there is a scheme `S`, an open `U` of `S` which is *not* retrocompact, and a surjective integral
morphism over `U`, which is the base change along `U ↪ S` of no surjective integral morphism over
`S`.

The witness is built in the module
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.MoreMorphisms.FppfApplication.IntegralExtensionCounterexample`
and its two companion modules: on `S = Spec (∏ (n : ℕ), ℤ)` and
`U = D(2, 2, …) ∪ ⋃ n, D(eₙ)`, it is the relative spectrum of the square-zero extension of
`𝒪_U` by the invertible ideal sheaf that is `𝒪` on `D(2, 2, …)` and `2 ^ n • ℤ` on `D(eₙ)`. That
ideal sheaf is not generated by its global sections, while the pushforward of an affine morphism
over the affine `S` always is after restriction to `U` — so no extension exists.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isIntegralHom_surjective_not_baseChange`: the counterexample.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.not_forall_exists_integral_surjective_extension`: the literal negation of
  Tag 0CNX for an arbitrary open subscheme. Equivalently, the hypothesis `[QuasiCompact U.ι]` of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_integral_surjective_extension` cannot be dropped.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_integral_surjective_extension_and_not_forall`: [Stacks, Tag 0CNX] in
  its corrected form — the extension exists over every retrocompact open, and the statement for
  an arbitrary open is false.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CNX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CNX)
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Stacks.IntegralExtensionCounterexample

universe u

/-- **A surjective integral morphism over a non-retrocompact open subscheme that is the base
change of nothing.** There are a scheme `S`, an open `U` of `S` that is not retrocompact in `S`
(that is, `U.ι` is not quasi-compact), and a surjective integral morphism `f` over `U`, such that
no integral morphism over `S` at all — surjective or not — has base change along `U ↪ S`
isomorphic to `f` over `U`. (Only affineness of the morphism over `S` is used, so this is
stronger than the failure of [Stacks, Tag 0CNX].) -/
theorem exists_isIntegralHom_surjective_not_baseChange :
    ∃ (S : Scheme.{u}) (U : S.Opens) (V : Scheme.{u}) (f : V ⟶ U.toScheme),
      ¬ QuasiCompact U.ι ∧ IsIntegralHom f ∧ Surjective f ∧
        ∀ (A : Scheme.{u}) (a : A ⟶ S), IsIntegralHom a →
          IsEmpty (Over.mk f ≅ (Over.pullback U.ι).obj (Over.mk a)) := by
  obtain ⟨G⟩ := nonempty_gluedCover.{u}
  refine ⟨Sch.{u}, Uo.{u}, G.carrier, G.str, not_quasiCompact_Uo, inferInstance, inferInstance,
    fun A a ha ↦ ⟨fun e ↦ ?_⟩⟩
  have := ha
  exact G.no_extension a e

/-- **The extension statement of [Stacks, Tag 0CNX] is false for an arbitrary open subscheme.**
So the hypothesis `[QuasiCompact U.ι]` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_integral_surjective_extension` — which says that `U` is retrocompact in
`S` — cannot be dropped. -/
theorem not_forall_exists_integral_surjective_extension :
    ¬ ∀ (S : Scheme.{u}) (U : S.Opens) (V : Scheme.{u}) (f : V ⟶ U.toScheme),
        IsIntegralHom f → Surjective f →
        ∃ (W : Scheme.{u}) (g : W ⟶ S), IsIntegralHom g ∧ Surjective g ∧
          Nonempty (Over.mk f ≅ (Over.pullback U.ι).obj (Over.mk g)) := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨S, U, V, f, -, hi, hs, hno⟩ := exists_isIntegralHom_surjective_not_baseChange.{u}
  obtain ⟨W, g, hgi, hgs, ⟨e⟩⟩ := h S U V f hi hs
  exact (hno W g hgi).false e

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0CNX, corrected.** The general statement of [Stacks, Tag 0CNX] is
false; this is its corrected (retrocompact) form, together with the failure of the general
statement.

1. Over a retrocompact open `U` of a scheme `S` (that is, `U.ι` quasi-compact), every surjective
   integral `f : V ⟶ U` is, as a scheme over `U`, the base change along `U ↪ S` of a surjective
   integral morphism `g : W ⟶ S`.
2. For an arbitrary open subscheme this fails: the statement of the tag as written, quantified
   over all schemes `S`, all opens `U`, and all surjective integral `f : V ⟶ U`, is false.
   The witness is `S = Spec (∏ (n : ℕ), ℤ)`, `U = D(2, 2, …) ∪ ⋃ n, D(eₙ)` for the standard
   idempotents `eₙ`, and `V` the relative spectrum over `U` of the square-zero extension of `𝒪_U`
   by an invertible ideal sheaf that is not generated by its global sections; any integral
   extension over the affine `S` would force that ideal sheaf to be globally generated.

The source's proof uses the relative normalization of `S` in `V`, which exists only when
`V ⟶ S` is quasi-compact and quasi-separated, i.e. when `U` is retrocompact; the second half
shows this restriction cannot be removed. -/
@[stacks 0CNX "the lemma as corrected in the errata: over every retrocompact open U of S a \
surjective integral V ⟶ U is the base change along U ↪ S of a surjective integral morphism \
over S, as schemes over U; and the statement for an arbitrary open U is false"]
theorem exists_integral_surjective_extension_and_not_forall :
    (∀ (S : Scheme.{u}) (U : S.Opens) [QuasiCompact U.ι] (V : Scheme.{u}) (f : V ⟶ U.toScheme)
        [IsIntegralHom f] [Surjective f],
        ∃ (W : Scheme.{u}) (g : W ⟶ S), IsIntegralHom g ∧ Surjective g ∧
          Nonempty (Over.mk f ≅ (Over.pullback U.ι).obj (Over.mk g))) ∧
      ¬ ∀ (S : Scheme.{u}) (U : S.Opens) (V : Scheme.{u}) (f : V ⟶ U.toScheme),
        IsIntegralHom f → Surjective f →
        ∃ (W : Scheme.{u}) (g : W ⟶ S), IsIntegralHom g ∧ Surjective g ∧
          Nonempty (Over.mk f ≅ (Over.pullback U.ι).obj (Over.mk g)) :=
  ⟨fun _ U _ _ f _ _ ↦ exists_integral_surjective_extension U f,
    not_forall_exists_integral_surjective_extension⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry
